me to despise anyone so  powerfully in such a short amount of  time and that is absolutely brilliant  because it forms a strong emotional bond  between now Fumi and the audience we are  bound together by our pure rage for this  character that I was so immediately  compelled to devour the rest of the  series and watch now for me hopefully  take revenge it was one of those rare  situations where I found my feelings  very much in sync with the protagonists  most of the time when now for me was  angry I was also furious be it at mine  or the king or whatever but my direct  feelings for being conveyed by now for  me on-screen and I think that's a pretty  powerful experience definitely not  something to be underestimated  so immediately shield hero succeeded  when many other yokai fail by providing  a main character I actually care about  as opposed to a more or less empty  vessel that I'm supposed to insert  myself into and live vicariously through  I mean now Fumi actually has a  personality that he's forced into very  quickly adapting to the role of  Gai which i thought was a great  direction to be taking him in a proper  underdog story where we actually have  the potential satisfaction of revenge as  well as the intense exploration of rage  unfortunately though this did not quite  last and as much as I was still on board  but now for me for the entirety of the  series eventually does slip into a more  conventional named protagonist role and  sadly he's not the only one that suffers  with time his counterpart heroes also  began the series with exceptional  potential but really they were all  completely outclassed by now for me in  no time at all and I think that mama  Yasu in particular was turned into just  a little bit too much of a dumbass like  there were points later on in the series  where it just became frustrating to  watch him confront now for me over and  over again on the basis of increasingly  obvious lies and the same goes for eat  Sookie and rent as well 